WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:05.440
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday. So I had a pretty big week last week. My novel The Fault in Our Stars returned to number 1 on the New York Times Bestseller List

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.840
56 weeks after it came out. Also,
my wife and I are expecting our second child,

00:00:08.849 --> 00:00:12.610
whom the President of the United
States told not to forget to be awesome,

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.000
but most importantly Hank,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.800
for the first time in American history, a sitting President of the United States

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.800
acknowledged that pennies are a terrible idea.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:24.020
He also acknowledged the penny is an excellent metaphor for what's wrong with government,

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.180
so yeah, it was an incredible
week! And in the wake of incredible weeks,

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:29.650
what I usually do is crawl into bed.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.910
I don't know why this is, Hank, but it's been happening my whole life. I just get overwhelmed with anxiety and

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.969
I decide I should crawl into bed and never do anything ever again

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:38.930
But that is a bad life strategy Hank, so today I'm going to update you on

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:40.190
12 things that we're doing.

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:43.520
1. 'mental_floss'. Hank, people often ask me how to get started as a writer. My advice is

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.180
always to find people who are also
starting out, and work with them. My first

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.200
writing gig ever in my life

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.649
was with 'mental_floss'. 10 years later, I'm talking to a camera for a living and

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:56.629
they've go on to become this educational and trivia empire, but they've never had a YouTube channel

00:00:56.629 --> 00:01:01.360
until now! Hank, you and I are both working on this, and I'm really excited to bring 'mental_floss' to YouTube.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.360
There's going to be list videos and quizzes, and like a cool intro, it's going to be great.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.680
Thing 2 - The Project for Awesome. So Hank, we still haven't announced which charities are getting
the money,

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.260
but that's because we don't know how much money there is going to be,

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.160
and we probably won't know for a couple more weeks,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.080
because we had to work with PayPal, and figure out how much shipping costs, and various other things.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.300
Thing 3 - The Fault in Our Stars movie? I'm not gonna lie to you,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.180
I've had my heart broken by Hollywood before, but I'm
starting to think that The Fault in Our Stars movie is

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:26.960
actually going to be a thing, so yeah.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.160
That said, please don't believe
everything that you read on the internet,

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:33.380
because journalists who work in Los
Angeles seem to just make things up.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:39.600
Rest assured, that when there is news, it will not come from, like, 'celebgossip.buzz', it will come from me.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.740
Thing 4 - DFTBA Records. Having taken over an abandoned nursery school in Missoula, Montana,

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:48.220
DFTBA Records is bigger and more awesome than ever!

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:53.160
We're continuing to try to make DFTBA more and more about getting cool stuff that also supports people you like,

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.840
whether that's a CGP Grey coffee mug, or a Wheezy Waiter T-shirt,

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:01.820
or a poster partly designed by a 16 year-old Norwegian girl named Asseal.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:05.280
Number 5 - My writing. I'm trying...

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.560
Number 6 - The Swindon Town Swoodilypoopers.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:15.540
Hank, the last FIFA 11 Swindon Town Swoodilypoopers video goes up tomorrow, when we will find out if we win the Barclays premiere league,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.760
and if the miracle of Swindon Town is complete! I just wanna go out and win it for the boys.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.880
By the way Hank, the actual Swindon Town football club is currently looking for a manager,

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:25.780
and I just wanna state for the record - I am available!

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:30.300
Number SEVEN: CrashCourse! Hank, you've just started teaching chemistry, which sounds very unpromising and yet,

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.780
it has been really entertaining and interesting and I am kind of learning.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:39.140
Meanwhile, I'm three episodes into teaching the history of Canada's pants, also known as the United States of America.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:45.940
Number 8 - VidCon 2013. Hank, most of the tickets to VidCon 2013 are gone, so if people want one they should get one now.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:51.780
VidCon's gonna be really fun this year. It will also be the first time that I leave the house after the birth of my kid so I will be ready to party.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:56.940
And by party, I mean sleep for 8 hours in a row. You know what I'm talking about, parents!

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:02.440
Number 9 - "The Lizzy Bennet Diaries". Hank, I get several e-mails a day, complimenting me on my excellent work for "The Lizzie Bennet" diaries,

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:06.800
which I don't do; I am not involved in that project at all. However, I am happy to take credit for it!

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:14.140
Number 10 - The kiva.org nerdfighters! Hank, the nerdfighters of kiva are approaching TWO MILLION dollars in loans to entrepreneurs in the developing world!

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:19.940
Number 11 - Parenting is still my biggest job at the moment and Number 12 - 2D-GLASSES,

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.420
which render 3-dimensional movies into crisp 2-dimensions.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:28.100
Hank, this idea that you had for 2-D glasses, which I thought was a terrible idea turns out to have been brilliant!

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:35.980
The '2-D glasses' Empire grows by the day. Hank, you have way too many ideas, but thank you for having them, because they pull me out of the quicksand of myself,

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.760
and force me to get to work. DFTBA, I will see you on Friday.

